  "notes": "The noun form {区切|くぎ}り is very common and often appears in the set phrase {区切|くぎ}りをつける (to bring something to a close, to draw a line).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {区切|くぎ}りをつける — to bring to a close, to draw a line\n- {一|ひと}つ{区切|くぎ}る — to pause/stop at one point\n- {文|ぶん}を{区切|くぎ}る — to break a sentence into parts\n- {段落|だんらく}で{区切|くぎ}る — to divide by paragraphs\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {分|わ}ける — to divide, to separate (more general)\n- {仕切|しき}る — to partition, to manage",
